Actually what I suggested was disregarding bones files left on the 
server by players who have never ascended on that server.  Less a 
matter of ensuring that bones are "fair" than that they are left by 
players who are more serious (and skilled) than a typical griefer. 

None of my solutions involve attempting to prevent someone from 
playing, or even from leaving griefer bones; I just want griefing 
to require a level of skill and commitment comparable to the games
the griefer is trying to disrupt. 

I definitely do not want manual identification of griefers.  I 
don't want to open the floor to politics, favoritism and fairness 
arguments. That crap sucks harder than griefing IMO. If it's not a 
rule that the server can enforce, one which treats everyone equally
and isn't unfair to those who don't complain, I am not interested 
in it. Arbitrary rules are better than rules that require or reward 
complaining. 

Anyway, people generally were not in favor of that solution, and if
they don't think it's a good idea I don't want to impose it on their 
playing experience. 

